\[\|\,\chi_{h}-\phi(h)\|_{2,\,h}\leqslant C_{3}|\phi(h)|_{2,\,2}\]

by virtue of Lemma 2.11 and

\[|\,\chi_{h}-\phi(h)|_{1,\,\Omega}\leqslant C_{4}h|\phi(h)|_{2,\,\Omega}\quad \text{by (A.21a)}.\]

In addition, since \(\phi(h)\!\in\!H^{2}(\Omega)\) and \(\partial\phi(h)\!/\partial n=0\) on \(\Gamma\) it follows that \(S(\partial\phi(h)\!/\partial n)=0\) and so

\[\|\,\phi(h)\|_{2,\,h}=|\phi(h)|_{2,\,\Omega}.\]

By collecting these inequalities we derive (2.65). 

_Remark 2.8_.: In the above proof, since \(\theta_{h}\) and \(\phi_{h}\) are related by (2.64), it follows from Lemma 2.5 that we have:

\[|\,\phi_{h}|_{1,\,s,\,\Omega}\leqslant C_{s}\,\|\,\theta_{h}\|_{0,\,\Omega} \quad\quad\forall\text{real }s\geqslant 2.\]

Therefore, under the assumptions of Lemma 2.12, in addition to (2.63), the following inf-sup condition holds:

